---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cycle Easy - Support"
  description="Get help with Cycle Easy, the privacy-first period tracker. FAQ and contact information."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/cycle-easy/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Cycle Easy?</p>
          <p>Check the FAQ below, or email us at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Cycle%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="faq-section">
            <h3 class="faq-category">Privacy & Security</h3>
            
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Is my period data really private?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes, absolutely. Cycle Easy stores all data locally on your device only. There are no servers, no cloud storage, no accounts, and no way for anyone — including us — to access your information. We built the app this way intentionally because we believe menstrual health data deserves the strongest possible privacy protections.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Can my data be subpoenaed or requested by law enforcement?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>We cannot produce data we don't have. Cycle Easy has no servers, no databases, and no user records. Your data exists only on your device. We literally cannot comply with data requests because we possess nothing to hand over. Your data is protected by your device's security and any legal protections that apply to your personal property.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">What about Apple HealthKit?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>HealthKit integration is completely optional and disabled by default. If you choose to enable it, Cycle Easy can write your cycle data to Apple Health — but this stays on your device, governed by Apple's privacy protections. We never see this data. You can disable HealthKit sync at any time in the app settings.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Does the app collect any analytics?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>No. Cycle Easy contains zero analytics, crash reporting, advertising, or third-party SDKs. We don't track how you use the app, which features are popular, or even how many people have downloaded it. We accept this trade-off because your privacy matters more than our metrics.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-section">
            <h3 class="faq-category">Using the App</h3>
            
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">How do I log my period?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>From the home screen, tap "Log Period" when your period starts. You can optionally record flow intensity (light, medium, heavy). When your period ends, tap "End Period." That's it — the app handles the rest.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">How accurate are the predictions?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Predictions improve over time as the app learns your unique cycle patterns. After 2-3 cycles, most users find predictions quite accurate. Remember that cycles naturally vary, so predictions are estimates, not certainties. The more consistently you log, the better predictions become.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">What symptoms can I track?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Cycle Easy lets you track cramps, mood, energy levels, headaches, breast tenderness, bloating, and more. Quick daily logging helps you spot patterns over time. All symptom data stays on your device like everything else.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">What about fertility tracking?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Cycle Easy includes optional fertility window estimates, but this feature is disabled by default and must be manually enabled. <strong>Important:</strong> These estimates are for awareness only and should NOT be used for contraception. The app includes clear disclaimers about this. Always consult healthcare providers for family planning decisions.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-section">
            <h3 class="faq-category">Data Management</h3>
            
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">How do I export my data?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Go to Settings → Export Data. You'll receive a JSON file containing all your cycle history, symptoms, and settings. This file is yours to keep, import elsewhere, or delete as you choose.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">How do I delete all my data?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Go to Settings → Delete All Data. This permanently erases everything from your device. Alternatively, simply uninstalling the app will delete all data. Since there's no cloud backup, deletion is truly permanent.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Can I transfer data to a new phone?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>If you restore your new phone from an encrypted device backup (via iTunes/Finder or iCloud), your Cycle Easy data will transfer. Otherwise, you'll start fresh on the new device. We intentionally don't offer cloud sync to protect your privacy.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">What happens if I lose my phone?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Your Cycle Easy data is protected by your device's passcode and biometric security (Face ID/Touch ID). If your phone is lost, your data remains encrypted. If you didn't have a backup, the data is gone — which, from a privacy perspective, can be a feature rather than a bug.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-section">
            <h3 class="faq-category">General</h3>
            
            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Is Cycle Easy free?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Yes, Cycle Easy is completely free with no subscriptions, no in-app purchases, and no ads. We believe privacy-first period tracking should be accessible to everyone.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Why don't you offer cloud backup?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>Cloud backup would require storing your data on servers — creating exactly the kind of centralized database we're trying to avoid. We believe the privacy benefits of local-only storage outweigh the convenience of cloud sync. Your encrypted device backups are a safer alternative.</p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary class="faq-question">Is this a medical device?</summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>No. Cycle Easy is a personal tracking tool, not a medical device. It should not be used for medical diagnosis, treatment decisions, or contraception. Always consult healthcare providers for medical concerns.</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </div>

        </div>

        <div class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-[var(--border-color)]">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-4">Still need help?</h2>
          <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Email us at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Cycle%20Easy%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a>. We typically respond within 24-48 hours.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .faq-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .faq-category {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent-primary, #e11d48);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e5e5e5);
    padding: 1rem 0;
  }

  .faq-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .faq-question {
    font-family: 'Satoshi', sans-serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary, #0a0a0a);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .faq-question::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-question::after {
    content: '+';
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary, #737373);
    transition: transform 0.2s;
  }

  details[open] .faq-question::after {
    content: '−';
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary, #737373);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .faq-answer p + p {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .faq-answer strong {
    color: var(--text-primary, #0a0a0a);
  }

  :global(.dark) .faq-question {
    color: var(--text-primary, #fafafa);
  }

  :global(.dark) .faq-answer strong {
    color: var(--text-primary, #fafafa);
  }
</style>
